    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "The SGD 5.00 no-show fee and the SGD 5.00 already refunded to the rider and withheld from the driver are held; this case must go to a human reviewer, because one fact the no-show rules need cannot be fixed on this record.\n\nTo the driver: on the evidence, your no-show looks procedurally sound. The trip record auto-arrived you at 09:21:45 and the nearest GPS fix was 1.81 m from the Block 680 pickup, well inside the 50 m arrival radius, with the trace reporting a continuous run of 0 kph fixes from 09:21:50 to 09:29:50 (POL-NS-21). This was an on-demand trip, so the 300 s free wait ran from your arrival and expired at 09:26:45; you cancelled at 09:30:10, 505 s after arrival. Before cancelling you sent three in-app messages (09:22:00, 09:25:30, 09:28:40) and placed two in-app calls (09:24:10, 09:27:20, both unanswered), so POL-NS-23's contact obligation is met, and the SGD 5.00 fee charged at 09:30:14 matches the policy fee (POL-NS-22).\n\nTo the rider: your account that the driver never came to your block is not corroborated by any rider-side trace — the only GPS on file is the driver's own device — and it does not displace the POL-NS-21 arrival test, which reads the trip record's arrival event corroborated by the GPS trace. That the messages were delivered and read does not establish that you boarded.\n\nWhy the case cannot be decided here: POL-NS-24 gives a rider a no-charge route where the driver failed to arrive by the scheduled pickup time plus five minutes. This booking was on-demand and the record carries no scheduled pickup time (scheduled_at is null; the derived driver deadline is null, reason 'on-demand trip: no scheduled time'), so that deadline cannot be fixed. POL-NS-24's own reading sends this situation to POL-GEN-26, and POL-GEN-26 requires the case to be escalated rather than an outcome inferred from the absence of evidence. The interim reversal at 10:46:10 is therefore neither confirmed nor undone here.\n\nNo referral issues: POL-NS-24's goodwill credit does not fire (the driver made contact), POL-NS-25's repeat no-show flag does not fire (the rider's count is 1, below the threshold of 3), and POL-NS-22's fee-amount check does not fire (the fee charged is the policy 5.00 SGD). Open question for the reviewer: whether an on-demand trip with no scheduled pickup time can support a POL-NS-24 no-charge route at all, and whether the rider's uncorroborated account should outweigh the driver's corroborated arrival."
  },
